{"name":"Top Hat Tan","hex":"#c1a393","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"top","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Papantla Totonac."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The highest or uppermost part of something.","The part of something that is usually highest or uppermost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/top"},{"term":"hat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Haitian Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covering for the head, often in the approximate form of a cone, dome or  cylinder closed at its top end, and sometimes having a brim and other decoration.","A particular role or capacity that a person might fill."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hat"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Top Hat","blocks":[{"text":"Top Hat is a 1935 American musical comedy film, in which Fred Astaire plays an American tap dancer named Jerry Travers, who arrives in London to star in a show produced by Horace Hardwick. He meets and attempts to impress Dale Tremont to win her affection. The film also features Eric Blore as Hardwick's valet Bates, Erik Rhodes as Alberto Beddini, a fashion designer and rival for Dale's affections, and Helen Broderick as Hardwick's long-suffering wife Madge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/TopHatORGI.jpg/330px-TopHatORGI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_Hat","wikidata":"Q1139031"},{"title":"Top hat","blocks":[{"text":"A top hat is a tall, flat-crowned hat traditionally associated with formal wear in Western dress codes, meaning white tie, morning dress, or frock coat. Traditionally made of black silk or sometimes grey, the top hat emerged in Western fashion by the end of the 18th century. Although such hats fell out of fashion through the 20th century, being almost entirely phased out by the time of the counterculture of the 1960s, it remains a formal fashion accessory. A collapsible variant of a top hat, developed in the 19th century, is known as an opera hat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/1910_top_hat.jpg/330px-1910_top_hat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_hat","wikidata":"Q110304"},{"title":"Hat","blocks":[{"text":"A hat is a head covering which is worn for various reasons, including protection against weather conditions, ceremonial reasons such as university graduation, religious reasons, comedy, safety, or as a fashion accessory. Hats which incorporate mechanical features, such as visors, spikes, flaps, braces or beer holders shade into the broader category of headgear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg/330px-Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hat","wikidata":"Q80151"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)","wikidata":"Q1670336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Top-Hat-Rogers-Astaire.jpg/500px-Top-Hat-Rogers-Astaire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Top-Hat-Rogers-Astaire.jpg/128